* APIOSEXECPROBE - may THIS session reach the operating system?
*
* 21 Aug 26 - SPLIT OUT OF APIADMINPROBE, and the reason is in that file's tail
* comment: this leg ABORTS when it is refused, and an abort discards the output
* an API session has captured.  Kept in the same program, it destroyed the
* $cred measurement every time the gate worked.  Run on its own, an abort costs
* nothing, because the ABSENCE of PROBE.WHOAMI is exactly what this measures.
*
* Copied into a throwaway account's BP by gplbld/verify-apiadmin.ps1, compiled
* there, and run TWICE: once from a local SD session and once down a real API
* connection.  THE COMPARISON IS THE MEASUREMENT.
*
* WHAT A REFUSAL LOOKS LIKE: k_error aborts the program, so nothing after the
* os.execute runs.  PROBE.OSEXEC.TRIED is printed BEFORE the attempt, so its
* presence separates "refused" from "never got there", and PROBE.WHOAMI is
* printed only if the call RETURNED.
*
* HARMLESS BY CHOICE: it reads an identity and changes nothing.  Do not be
* tempted to make it write something to prove the point harder.

program apiosexecprobe

   crt 'PROBE.OSEXEC.TRIED=YES'

   who.out = ''
   os.execute 'cmd /c whoami' capturing who.out

   * FLATTENED TO ONE TOKEN.  The reply is "nt authority\system" - a SPACE and
   * a BACKSLASH - and the caller reads these markers with one regex per line,
   * so both separators have to go or the marker is truncated at the space and
   * read as "nt".
   *
   * 21 Aug 26 - THE BACKSLASH WAS NOT IN THIS LIST AND SHOULD HAVE BEEN.  The
   * convert listed char(10), char(13), @fm, @vm and space only, so the marker
   * came out as "nt_authority\system" while verify-apiadmin.ps1 matched on
   * ^nt_authority_+system$ - which does not match a backslash.  The result was
   * a FALSE PASS on the most important check in that script: the session
   * reported itself LocalSystem and the verdict read "API session is NOT
   * running as SYSTEM".  The reason it was caught at all is that the raw
   * marker is printed in the transcript beside the verdict.
   * char(92) RATHER THAN A LITERAL BACKSLASH: this BASIC accepts \ as a string
   * delimiter alongside ' and ", so a bare backslash in a source line is a
   * shape worth not relying on.
   who.line = who.out
   convert char(10):char(13):@fm:@vm:' ':char(92) to '______' in who.line
   who.line = trim(who.line, '_', 'B')

   if who.line = '' then
      crt 'PROBE.WHOAMI=NONE'
   end else
      crt 'PROBE.WHOAMI=' : who.line
   end

end
